        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "227053fa-ad88-5c33-82a4-b55835012ad0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Albany International Airport, Dane County Regional Airport, Albany, Madison, Albany County, New York, Wisconsin, Colonie\n- Products: Interstate 687, I-90, I-87\n\nFacts:\n- Albany International Airport is a public airport located seven miles northwest of Albany in Albany County, New York, United States.\n- Albany International Airport has the codes IATA ALB, ICAO KALB, and FAA LID ALB.\n- Dane County Regional Airport, also called Truax Field, is a civil-military airport located six miles northeast of downtown Madison, Wisconsin.\n- Dane County Regional Airport has the codes IATA MSN, ICAO KMSN, and FAA LID MSN.\n- Interstate 687 was a proposed highway that would have connected I-90 in Albany to I-87 near Albany International Airport in Colonie.",
